{title: A Mighty Fortress Is Our God}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
A [C]mighty [G]fortress [Am]is our [G]God, a [Em]bulwark [C]never [Dm]fai-[C]ling
Our [C]helper [G]He, a[Am]mid the [G]flood, of [Em]mortal [C]ills pre[Dm]vai-[C]ling
For [G]still our [D]ancient [G]foe[**], doth [**]seek to [F]work us [Am]woe[**]
His [Am]craft and [A]power are [G]great[**], and, [F]armed with [A]cruel [E]hate[**]
On [Em]earth is [C]not his [Dm]e-[C]qual.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Did [C]we in [G]our own [Am]strength con[G]fide, our [Em]striving [C]would be [Dm]los-[C]ing
Were [C]not the [G]right Man [Am]on our [G]side, the [Em]Man of [C]God's own [Dm]choo-[C]sing
You [G]ask who [D]that may [G]be[**]? Christ [**]Jesus, [F]it is [Am]he[**]
Lord [Am]Saba-[A]oth his [G]name[**], from [F]age to [A]age the [E]same[**]
And [Em]he must [C]win the [Dm]bat-[C]tle.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [C]tho this [G]world, with [Am]devils [G]filled, should [Em]threaten [C]to un[Dm]do [C]us
We [C]will not [G]fear, for [Am]God has [G]willed his [Em]truth to [C]triumph [Dm]through [C]us
The [G]prince of [D]darkness [G]grim[**], we [**]tremble [F]not for [Am]him[**]
His [Am]rage we [A]can en[G]dure[**], for [F]lo! his [A]doom is [E]sure[**]
One [Em]little [C]word shall [Dm]fell [C]him.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
That [C]Word a[G]bove all [Am]earthly [G]powers; no [Em]thanks to [C]them a[Dm]bi-[C]deth
The [C]Spirit [G]and the [Am]gifts are [G]ours through [Em]him who [C]with us [Dm]si-[C]deth
Let [G]goods and [D]kindred [G]go[**], this [**]mortal [F]life al[Am]so[**]
The [Am]body [A]they may [G]kill[**]: God's [F]truth a[A]bideth [E]still[**]
His [Em]kingdom [C]is for-[Dm]e-[C]ver.
{end_of_verse}
